-- Step 32: receipts from customers, and the cheques among them.
-- track: A
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A receipt is a draft the app writes: who paid, how much, how (cash, into a bank account, or
-- by cheque) and which unpaid invoices it pays. It is posted once, by a function of the
-- database's own, which takes the number and posts the journal:
--
--   debit   the cash or bank account            what reached it
--   debit   Bank charges                        what the bank kept on the way, if anything
--   debit   Cheques in hand                     instead of the two above, for a cheque
--   credit  Trade receivables (the customer)    what the receipt pays of invoices
--   credit  Advances from customers (the same)  what it pays beyond them
--
-- A cheque then moves on, each step an act of the database's own: deposited (no entry in the
-- books: it is still a cheque), cleared (bank and bank charges against Cheques in hand), or
-- bounced, which reverses what the receipt posted and leaves the invoices unpaid again (a
-- cheque that had cleared first comes back out of the bank in full; what the bank kept for
-- collecting it stays an expense). A receipt entered by mistake is cancelled the same way.
-- Part of an advance is set against an invoice later with a journal that moves it from
-- advances to the customer's account.
--
-- The app's role cannot write a receipt's status, number or journals, nor where its cheque
-- stands, nor mark an allocation as counting: it has no right to those columns. A posted
-- receipt and what it pays never change except through the functions below.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE100 to SE199 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE100  no such receipt in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE101  the receipt or its cheque is not in the state this needs
--   SE102  an invoice named is not this customer's, not posted, or has less left to pay
--   SE103  the receipt pays more than it holds
--   SE104  a posted receipt is never changed or removed
--   SE105  what a receipt pays is written only while the receipt is a draft
--   SE106  the money goes into a cash account for cash and a bank account otherwise
--   SE107  receipts are posted in read committed transactions
--   SE108  the dates are out of order
--   SE109  opening balances that receipts have been set against are not reversed
--   SE110  more than is left of the advance
--   SE111  a date that has not come yet: nothing is recorded before it happens

